      { s: "", jp: "{去年|きょねん}は{大|おお}きな{悩|なや}みだと{思|おも}っていたことが、{今|いま}の{私|わたし}にはほとんど{思|おも}い{出|だ}せないほど{小|ちい}さなことだったりする。", ro: "Kyonen wa ōkina nayami da to omotte ita koto ga, ima no watashi ni wa hotondo omoidasenai hodo chiisana koto datta risuru.", en: "Things I thought were big worries last year turn out to be so small that I can hardly remember them now." },
      { s: "", jp: "{逆|ぎゃく}に、{何気|なにげ}なく{書|か}いた{一言|ひとこと}が、{今|いま}では{大切|たいせつ}な{思|おも}い{出|で}になっていることもある。", ro: "Gyaku ni, nanigenaku kaita hitokoto ga, ima de wa taisetsuna omoide ni natte iru koto mo aru.", en: "Conversely, a casual remark I wrote can now have become a precious memory." },
      { s: "", jp: "{旅行|りょこう}の{日|ひ}は{短|みじか}い{言葉|ことば}でも、{読|よ}み{返|かえ}せばその{日|ひ}の{景色|けしき}が{浮|う}かんでくる。", ro: "Ryokō no hi wa mijikai kotoba de mo, yomikaesebaso no hi no keshiki ga ukande kuru.", en: "Even short words on a trip day bring back that day's scenery when I read them again." },
      { s: "", jp: "{毎日|まいにち}{少|すこ}しだけ{続|つづ}けることで、{時間|じかん}の{流|なが}れを{目|め}で{確|たし}かめられるのが、この{日記|にっき}のみりょくだと{思|おも}う。", ro: "Mainichi sukoshi dake tsuzukeru koto de, jikan no nagare o me de tashikamerareru no ga, kono nikki no miryoku da to omou.", en: "I think the charm of this diary is that by continuing a little each day, you can see the flow of time with your own eyes." }
